```python
# Code-1
class Foo(Generic[T]):
    def __init__(self, a: int):
        self.a = a


class Bar(Foo[int]):
    pass

# Code-2
class Foo(Generic[T]):
    pass


class Bar(Foo[int]):
    def __init__(self, a: int):
        self.a = a

# Code-3
class Foo(Generic[T]):
    def __init__(self, a: int):
        self.a = a


class Bar(Foo[int]):
    def __init__(self):
        pass
```

| Code | Python 3.8 | Python 3.9 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Code-1 | `args`, `kwds` | `a` |
| Code-2 | `args`, `kwds` | `a` |
| Code-3 | `args`, `kwds` | none |

With the above three variants of code, Python 3.9 always works as expected, however Python 3.8 always behave the same.
